---
# day10 worker on navajo. 16 jobs at once: the guest has 32 vCPUs and 200G,
# and a day10 job is one process container at a time, so this is a bet on
# builds being I/O-bound more often than CPU-bound. Watch D: - every job
# adds layers to the cache, and the prune threshold is what keeps it in
# check.
day10_capacity: 16

# Registers with the scheduler, and names its Windows service, as navajo:
# one day10 worker per host, so the host's name is the useful one.
worker_name: navajo
